module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.NaiveCotangentRelativeDegreeZero
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.NaiveCotangent.JacobiZariskiCokernel

/-!
# The stalk morphisms of canonical presentations are the tower morphisms of Stacks 07VC

Let `A ⟶ B ⟶ C` be morphisms of sheaves of commutative rings on a topological space and let `z`
be a point.  The stalk of the naive cotangent complex is the naive cotangent complex of the
canonical presentation of the stalk (Stacks 0D09), and the stalks of the two canonical maps `c₁`
and `g` of Stacks 0E1Y are the ring-level comparisons
`NaiveCotangent.nlExtensionBaseChangeMap` and `NaiveCotangent.nlExtensionOverMap` of two
morphisms of canonical presentations of the stalk rings,
`Stacks.NaiveCotangentTowerStalk.stalkTowerHomBase` and `stalkTowerHomRel`
(`Stacks.NaiveCotangentStalkJacobiZariski.stalkLegNegOneLinear_spaceBaseChangeMap` and its three
companions).

Those two morphisms are built from a commutative square of sheaves, and they are transported
along `Stacks.NaiveCotangentTowerStalk.homCongrEq` so that the comparison algebra structure read
off the stalk of an identity morphism is replaced by the identity one.  The ring-level results
about a tower of rings, by contrast, are stated at the two explicit morphisms of canonical
presentations `NaiveCotangent.towerMidHom`, `[b] ↦ [φ(b)]`, and `NaiveCotangent.towerTopHom`,
`[c] ↦ [c]`.

**The two families are the same morphisms.**  Both act on coefficients by the stalk of the
structural morphism and send a variable to the variable indexed by its image, so they have the
same underlying map of polynomial rings, and a morphism of extensions is determined by that map.
Consequently every ring-level statement at `NaiveCotangent.towerMidHom` and
`NaiveCotangent.towerTopHom` applies verbatim to what the stalk lemmas deliver — in particular
`NaiveCotangent.bijective_towerCokernelMap`, which is stated at those two morphisms and not at
arbitrary ones, unlike `NaiveCotangent.jacobiZariski_sixTerm_exact_canonical`.

The transport along `homCongrEq` costs nothing here:
`Stacks.NaiveCotangentStalkJacobiZariski.toRingHom_homCongrEq` says it does not change the
underlying ring homomorphism, so the whole comparison is the equality of two maps of polynomial
rings, checked on coefficients and on variables.

## Main results

* `Stacks.NaiveCotangentTowerStalk.stalkTowerHomBase_eq` and `stalkTowerHomRel_eq`: the two
  morphisms of canonical presentations of the stalks are `NaiveCotangent.towerMidHom` and
  `NaiveCotangent.towerTopHom`; `stalkTowerHom_eq` is the composite.
* `Stacks.NaiveCotangentTowerStalk.nlExtensionBaseChangeMap_stalkTowerHomBase` and
  `nlExtensionOverMap_stalkTowerHomRel`: hence the stalks of `c₁` and of `g` are the ring-level
  comparisons of those two morphisms, as chain maps.
* `Stacks.NaiveCotangentTowerStalk.cotangentMap_stalkTowerHomRel` and
  `range_cotangentMap_stalkTowerHomRel`: hence the
  cokernel of the stalk of `g` in degree `-1` is `NaiveCotangent.towerRelConormalCokernel`, the
  target of `NaiveCotangent.towerCokernelMap`.
* `Stacks.NaiveCotangentTowerStalk.exists_towerNullHomotopy_add_stalk` and
  `Stacks.NaiveCotangentTowerStalk.mem_range_baseChange_cotangentComplex_of_mem_range_stalk`:
  **the two elementwise halves of the remaining step of Stacks 0E1Y at a stalk**, obtained from
  `NaiveCotangent.bijective_towerCokernelMap` through those identifications.  The first says that
  `J/J²` is generated by the values of the homotopy of Stacks 07VC together with the image of the
  stalk of `g` in degree `-1`; the second that a combination of the `d X_b` whose image under the
  homotopy lies in that image is a boundary.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E1Y](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E1Y), the two canonical maps.
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07VC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07VC), the explicit homotopy
  whose induced map on cokernels is the remaining step.
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07BL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07BL), the canonical
  presentation.
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0D09](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0D09), the stalk of the naive
  cotangent complex.
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.NaiveCotangentAffineStalkLegs
open Stacks.NaiveCotangentTowerStalk
open Stacks.RelativeDifferentialStalk (algebraStalk)
open Stacks.Sites.Conormal (stalkIsScalarTowerSquareTarget)
open scoped TensorProduct

universe u

noncomputable section

namespace Stacks.NaiveCotangentTowerStalk

-- `Algebra.Generators.toExtension` is a plain definition, so the elaborator will not identify
-- `P.toExtension.Ring` with `P.Ring` at `implicit` transparency, and the comparison below is a
-- statement about the underlying polynomial rings.
attribute [local implicit_reducible] Algebra.Generators.toExtension

attribute [local instance 1]
  Sheaf.hasWeakSheafifyCommRingCat
  Sheaf.hasSheafifyAddCommGrpCat
  Sheaf.wEqualsLocallyBijectiveAddCommGrpCat

variable {T : TopCat.{u}}
  (A B C : CategoryTheory.Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology T) CommRingCat.{u})
  (a : A ⟶ B) (b : B ⟶ C) (z : T)

/-! ### The two morphisms of canonical presentations -/

/-- The algebra structure of the stalk of an identity morphism is the identity. -/
private theorem algebraMap_algebraStalk_id
    (X : CategoryTheory.Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology T) CommRingCat.{u})
    (r : ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk X.obj z)) :
    @algebraMap (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk X.obj z))
      (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk X.obj z)) _ _
      (algebraStalk (CategoryTheory.InducedCategory.Hom.hom (𝟙 X)) z) r = r := by
  rw [algebraStalk_id X z]; rfl

/-- **The morphism `Aₓ[Bₓ] ⟶ Aₓ[Cₓ]` of canonical presentations of the stalks attached to the
base-change factor of the tower is `NaiveCotangent.towerMidHom`.**  Both act as the identity on
coefficients and send the variable `X_β` to the variable `X_{bₓ β}`. -/
theorem stalkTowerHomBase_eq :
    letI := algebraStalk a.hom z
    letI := algebraStalk (a ≫ b).hom z
    letI := algebraStalk b.hom z
    letI := stalkIsScalarTowerSquareTarget A B C a (a ≫ b) b z rfl
    stalkTowerHomBase A B C a b z =
      (NaiveCotangent.towerMidHom (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk A.obj z))
          (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk B.obj z))
          (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk C.obj z))).toExtensionHom := by
  let := algebraStalk a.hom z
  let := algebraStalk (a ≫ b).hom z
  let := algebraStalk b.hom z
  let := algebraStalk (CategoryTheory.InducedCategory.Hom.hom (𝟙 A)) z
  let := stalkIsScalarTowerSquareTarget A B C a (a ≫ b) b z rfl
  refine Algebra.Extension.Hom.ext ?_
  rw [show stalkTowerHomBase A B C a b z =
      homCongrEq (algebraStalk (CategoryTheory.InducedCategory.Hom.hom (𝟙 A)) z) (Algebra.id _)
        (algebraStalk b.hom z) (algebraStalk b.hom z) (algebraStalk_id A z) rfl
        (generatorsSelfStalkHomOfSquare A A B C a (a ≫ b) (𝟙 A) b z
          (Category.id_comp (a ≫ b)).symm) from rfl,
    Stacks.NaiveCotangentStalkJacobiZariski.toRingHom_homCongrEq,
    generatorsSelfStalkHomOfSquare_toRingHom]
  refine MvPolynomial.ringHom_ext (fun r => ?_) (fun i => ?_)
  · simp [Stacks.NaiveCotangentAffineComparison.squareRingHom, algebraMap_algebraStalk_id z A,
      Algebra.Generators.Hom.toAlgHom, MvPolynomial.algebraMap_eq]
  · simp [Stacks.NaiveCotangentAffineComparison.squareRingHom,
      Algebra.Generators.Hom.toAlgHom]

/-- **The morphism `Aₓ[Cₓ] ⟶ Bₓ[Cₓ]` of canonical presentations of the stalks attached to the
relative factor of the tower is `NaiveCotangent.towerTopHom`.**  Both act on coefficients by
`aₓ : Aₓ ⟶ Bₓ` and fix the variables. -/
theorem stalkTowerHomRel_eq :
    letI := algebraStalk a.hom z
    letI := algebraStalk (a ≫ b).hom z
    letI := algebraStalk b.hom z
    letI := stalkIsScalarTowerSquareTarget A B C a (a ≫ b) b z rfl
    stalkTowerHomRel A B B C a b a b z rfl =
      (NaiveCotangent.towerTopHom (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk A.obj z))
          (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk B.obj z))
          (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk C.obj z))).toExtensionHom := by
  let := algebraStalk a.hom z
  let := algebraStalk (a ≫ b).hom z
  let := algebraStalk b.hom z
  let := algebraStalk (CategoryTheory.InducedCategory.Hom.hom (𝟙 C)) z
  let := stalkIsScalarTowerSquareTarget A B C a (a ≫ b) b z rfl
  refine Algebra.Extension.Hom.ext ?_
  rw [show stalkTowerHomRel A B B C a b a b z rfl =
      homCongrEq (algebraStalk a.hom z) (algebraStalk a.hom z)
        (algebraStalk (CategoryTheory.InducedCategory.Hom.hom (𝟙 C)) z) (Algebra.id _) rfl
        (algebraStalk_id C z)
        (generatorsSelfStalkHomOfSquare A B C C (a ≫ b) b a (𝟙 C) z
          (Stacks.SheafOfModules.comp_id_eq_of_tower A B B C a b a b rfl)) from rfl,
    Stacks.NaiveCotangentStalkJacobiZariski.toRingHom_homCongrEq,
    generatorsSelfStalkHomOfSquare_toRingHom]
  refine MvPolynomial.ringHom_ext (fun r => ?_) (fun i => ?_)
  · simp [Stacks.NaiveCotangentAffineComparison.squareRingHom,
      Algebra.Generators.Hom.toAlgHom]
  · simp [Stacks.NaiveCotangentAffineComparison.squareRingHom, algebraMap_algebraStalk_id z C,
      Algebra.Generators.Hom.toAlgHom]

/-- **The composite morphism `Aₓ[Bₓ] ⟶ Bₓ[Cₓ]` of canonical presentations of the stalks** is the
composite of `NaiveCotangent.towerTopHom` with `NaiveCotangent.towerMidHom`, which is the
morphism whose difference with `NaiveCotangent.towerConstHom` is the homotopy of Stacks
07VC. -/
theorem stalkTowerHom_eq :
    letI := algebraStalk a.hom z
    letI := algebraStalk (a ≫ b).hom z
    letI := algebraStalk b.hom z
    letI := stalkIsScalarTowerSquareTarget A B C a (a ≫ b) b z rfl
    stalkTowerHom A B B C a b a b z rfl =
      (NaiveCotangent.towerTopHom (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk A.obj z))
            (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk B.obj z))
            (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk C.obj z))).toExtensionHom.comp
        (NaiveCotangent.towerMidHom (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk A.obj z))
          (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk B.obj z))
          (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk C.obj z))).toExtensionHom := by
  let := algebraStalk a.hom z
  let := algebraStalk (a ≫ b).hom z
  let := algebraStalk b.hom z
  let := stalkIsScalarTowerSquareTarget A B C a (a ≫ b) b z rfl
  rw [show stalkTowerHom A B B C a b a b z rfl =
      (stalkTowerHomRel A B B C a b a b z rfl).comp (stalkTowerHomBase A B C a b z) from rfl,
    stalkTowerHomRel_eq A B C a b z, stalkTowerHomBase_eq A B C a b z]

/-! ### The stalks of the two canonical maps of Stacks 0E1Y -/

/-- **The stalk of the canonical map `c₁` of Stacks 0E1Y is the ring-level comparison of
`NaiveCotangent.towerMidHom`**, as a chain map.  Together with
`Stacks.NaiveCotangentStalkJacobiZariski.stalkLegNegOneLinear_spaceBaseChangeMap` and its degree
`0` companion this identifies the stalk of `c₁` with a comparison of the canonical
presentations stated at the explicit morphism of Stacks 07VC. -/
theorem nlExtensionBaseChangeMap_stalkTowerHomBase :
    letI := algebraStalk a.hom z
    letI := algebraStalk (a ≫ b).hom z
    letI := algebraStalk b.hom z
    letI := stalkIsScalarTowerSquareTarget A B C a (a ≫ b) b z rfl
    NaiveCotangent.nlExtensionBaseChangeMap
        (T := ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk C.obj z)) (stalkTowerHomBase A B C a b z) =
      NaiveCotangent.towerBaseChangeMap (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk A.obj z))
        (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk B.obj z))
        (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk C.obj z)) := by
  exact congrArg _ (stalkTowerHomBase_eq A B C a b z)

/-- **The stalk of the canonical map `g` of Stacks 0E1Y is the ring-level comparison of
`NaiveCotangent.towerTopHom`**, as a chain map. -/
theorem nlExtensionOverMap_stalkTowerHomRel :
    letI := algebraStalk a.hom z
    letI := algebraStalk (a ≫ b).hom z
    letI := algebraStalk b.hom z
    letI := stalkIsScalarTowerSquareTarget A B C a (a ≫ b) b z rfl
    NaiveCotangent.nlExtensionOverMap (stalkTowerHomRel A B B C a b a b z rfl) =
      NaiveCotangent.towerRelMap (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk A.obj z))
        (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk B.obj z))
        (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk C.obj z)) := by
  exact congrArg _ (stalkTowerHomRel_eq A B C a b z)

/-- **The stalk of `g` in degree `-1` is `Algebra.Extension.Cotangent.map` of
`NaiveCotangent.towerTopHom`.**  This is the degree `-1` component of
`Stacks.NaiveCotangentTowerStalk.nlExtensionOverMap_stalkTowerHomRel` in the native spelling:
a `NaiveCotangent.TwoTerm` carries its module structures as fields, so a goal mentioning
`.f₁` carries the field projection rather than the native instance on
`Algebra.Extension.Cotangent`, and `rw` does not see through it. -/
theorem cotangentMap_stalkTowerHomRel :
    letI := algebraStalk a.hom z
    letI := algebraStalk (a ≫ b).hom z
    letI := algebraStalk b.hom z
    letI := stalkIsScalarTowerSquareTarget A B C a (a ≫ b) b z rfl
    Algebra.Extension.Cotangent.map (stalkTowerHomRel A B B C a b a b z rfl) =
      Algebra.Extension.Cotangent.map
        (NaiveCotangent.towerTopHom (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk A.obj z))
          (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk B.obj z))
          (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk C.obj z))).toExtensionHom := by
  exact congrArg _ (stalkTowerHomRel_eq A B C a b z)

/-- **The stalk of `g` in degree `0` is `Algebra.Extension.CotangentSpace.map` of
`NaiveCotangent.towerTopHom`.** -/
theorem cotangentSpaceMap_stalkTowerHomRel :
    letI := algebraStalk a.hom z
    letI := algebraStalk (a ≫ b).hom z
    letI := algebraStalk b.hom z
    letI := stalkIsScalarTowerSquareTarget A B C a (a ≫ b) b z rfl
    Algebra.Extension.CotangentSpace.map (stalkTowerHomRel A B B C a b a b z rfl) =
      Algebra.Extension.CotangentSpace.map
        (NaiveCotangent.towerTopHom (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk A.obj z))
          (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk B.obj z))
          (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk C.obj z))).toExtensionHom := by
  exact congrArg _ (stalkTowerHomRel_eq A B C a b z)

/-- **The cokernel of the stalk of `g` in degree `-1` is
`NaiveCotangent.towerRelConormalCokernel`**, the target of
`NaiveCotangent.towerCokernelMap`. -/
theorem range_cotangentMap_stalkTowerHomRel :
    letI := algebraStalk a.hom z
    letI := algebraStalk (a ≫ b).hom z
    letI := algebraStalk b.hom z
    letI := stalkIsScalarTowerSquareTarget A B C a (a ≫ b) b z rfl
    LinearMap.range (Algebra.Extension.Cotangent.map
          (stalkTowerHomRel A B B C a b a b z rfl)) =
      LinearMap.range (Algebra.Extension.Cotangent.map
        (NaiveCotangent.towerTopHom (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk A.obj z))
          (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk B.obj z))
          (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk C.obj z))).toExtensionHom) := by
  exact congrArg _ (cotangentMap_stalkTowerHomRel A B C a b z)

/-! ### The remaining step of Stacks 0E1Y at a stalk, elementwise -/

/-- **`J/J²` is generated by the values of the homotopy of Stacks 07VC together with the image of
the stalk of `g` in degree `-1`.**  This is the surjectivity half of
`NaiveCotangent.bijective_towerCokernelMap`, read at the morphisms of canonical presentations
that the stalk lemmas of Stacks 0E1Y deliver. -/
theorem exists_towerNullHomotopy_add_stalk
    (j : letI := algebraStalk b.hom z
      (Algebra.Generators.self (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk B.obj z))
        (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk C.obj z))).toExtension.Cotangent) :
    letI := algebraStalk a.hom z
    letI := algebraStalk (a ≫ b).hom z
    letI := algebraStalk b.hom z
    letI := stalkIsScalarTowerSquareTarget A B C a (a ≫ b) b z rfl
    ∃ (n : ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk C.obj z) ⊗[ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk B.obj z)]
          (Algebra.Generators.self (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk A.obj z))
            (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk B.obj z))).toExtension.CotangentSpace)
        (w : (Algebra.Generators.self (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk A.obj z))
          (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk C.obj z))).toExtension.Cotangent),
      NaiveCotangent.towerNullHomotopyBaseChange (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk A.obj z))
            (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk B.obj z))
            (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk C.obj z)) n +
          Algebra.Extension.Cotangent.map (stalkTowerHomRel A B B C a b a b z rfl) w = j := by
  let := algebraStalk a.hom z
  let := algebraStalk (a ≫ b).hom z
  let := algebraStalk b.hom z
  let := stalkIsScalarTowerSquareTarget A B C a (a ≫ b) b z rfl
  obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ := NaiveCotangent.surjective_towerCokernelMap
    (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk A.obj z)) (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk B.obj z))
    (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk C.obj z))
    ((LinearMap.range (Algebra.Extension.Cotangent.map
      (NaiveCotangent.towerTopHom (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk A.obj z))
        (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk B.obj z))
        (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk C.obj z))).toExtensionHom)).mkQ j)
  obtain ⟨n, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mkQ_surjective (LinearMap.range
    ((Algebra.Generators.self (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk A.obj z))
      (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk B.obj z))).toExtension.cotangentComplex.baseChange
        (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk C.obj z)))) q
  rw [NaiveCotangent.towerCokernelMap_mkQ, Submodule.mkQ_apply, Submodule.mkQ_apply,
    Submodule.Quotient.eq] at hq
  obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := hq
  refine ⟨n, -w, ?_⟩
  rw [cotangentMap_stalkTowerHomRel A B C a b z, map_neg, hw]
  abel

/-- **A combination of the `d X_b` whose image under the homotopy of Stacks 07VC lies in the
image of the stalk of `g` in degree `-1` is a boundary.**  This is the injectivity half of
`NaiveCotangent.bijective_towerCokernelMap`, read at the morphisms of canonical presentations
that the stalk lemmas of Stacks 0E1Y deliver. -/
theorem mem_range_baseChange_cotangentComplex_of_mem_range_stalk
    (n : letI := algebraStalk a.hom z
      letI := algebraStalk b.hom z
      ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk C.obj z) ⊗[ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk B.obj z)]
        (Algebra.Generators.self (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk A.obj z))
          (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk B.obj z))).toExtension.CotangentSpace)
    (hn : letI := algebraStalk a.hom z
      letI := algebraStalk (a ≫ b).hom z
      letI := algebraStalk b.hom z
      letI := stalkIsScalarTowerSquareTarget A B C a (a ≫ b) b z rfl
      NaiveCotangent.towerNullHomotopyBaseChange (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk A.obj z))
          (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk B.obj z))
          (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk C.obj z)) n ∈
        LinearMap.range (Algebra.Extension.Cotangent.map
          (stalkTowerHomRel A B B C a b a b z rfl))) :
    letI := algebraStalk a.hom z
    letI := algebraStalk b.hom z
    n ∈ LinearMap.range
      ((Algebra.Generators.self (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk A.obj z))
        (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk B.obj z))).toExtension.cotangentComplex.baseChange
          (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk C.obj z))) := by
  let := algebraStalk a.hom z
  let := algebraStalk (a ≫ b).hom z
  let := algebraStalk b.hom z
  let := stalkIsScalarTowerSquareTarget A B C a (a ≫ b) b z rfl
  rw [cotangentMap_stalkTowerHomRel A B C a b z] at hn
  have h0 : NaiveCotangent.towerCokernelMap (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk A.obj z))
      (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk B.obj z)) (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk C.obj z))
      ((LinearMap.range
        ((Algebra.Generators.self (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk A.obj z))
          (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk B.obj z))).toExtension.cotangentComplex.baseChange
            (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk C.obj z)))).mkQ n) = 0 := by
    rw [NaiveCotangent.towerCokernelMap_mkQ, Submodule.mkQ_apply,
      Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero]
    exact hn
  have := (injective_iff_map_eq_zero _).1 (NaiveCotangent.injective_towerCokernelMap
    (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk A.obj z)) (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk B.obj z))
    (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk C.obj z))) _ h0
  rwa [Submodule.mkQ_apply, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero] at this

end Stacks.NaiveCotangentTowerStalk

end

end
